{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfu9PvYVzALchVu2q7Kyy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The dashboard and the alert rule both exist. I haven't opened the dashboard to check the panels render, and the rule hasn't run yet, so it hasn't been tested.\n\n**Data.** The logs data view has a `timestamp` time field. The fields that matter here are `response` (a string, so I used `response.keyword`), `bytes`, `extension`, `clientip`, `geo.src` and `geo.dest`, `machine.os`, `host`, `url` and `request`.\n\n**Dashboard.** \"EFF-a795e3fc Web logs overview\" has four panels:\n- **Total requests:** a single count.\n- **Requests over time:** a line chart of the count by `timestamp`.\n- **Responses by status code:** a pie chart of the count by `response.keyword`.\n- **Average bytes by extension:** a bar chart of average `bytes` per `extension.keyword`.\n\nMy first create call failed because the time-series panel needed an explicit time field. I fixed that and the second call succeeded.\n\nLink: http://localhost:15601/app/dashboards#/view/eff-a795e3fc-web-logs-overview-e35d2df3f089\n\n**Alert rule.** \"EFF-a795e3fc 5xx spike\" (id `eae8fc5f-53b2-45b0-8385-25023aa090fc`) is an Elasticsearch query rule on `kibana_sample_data_logs`. It runs every minute and fires when more than 10 documents with `response.keyword` starting with \"5\" arrive in the last 5 minutes.\n\nThe rule was created disabled by default, so I enabled it. The sample data is static, so it may not match any 5xx requests in the last 5 minutes. The rule also has no action attached, so it won't send a notification."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":984,"cache_read_input_tokens":20341,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":984},"output_tokens":571,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transfo